CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*thinkpad)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct thinkpad_wmi)...)
#1377: FILE: drivers/platform/x86/thinkpad-wmi.c:1135:
+	thinkpad = kzalloc(sizeof(struct thinkpad_wmi), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

